From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Strix Halo Packaging <packaging@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Backport: gate per-request multimodal processor and media IO kwargs

Upstream: vllm-project/vllm#58830, "[Security] Gate per-request multimodal
processor kwargs", merge commit 31f2e70cd3e403aaa471fb7fe3d33a7207aaf3cc
(main, 2026-09-26, first released in v0.31.0).

API server endpoints now reject a non-empty per-request mm_processor_kwargs
or media_io_kwargs with a validation error unless the server is started with
--trust-request-mm-kwargs. Those arguments change media loading, sizing,
sampling and preprocessing, so an untrusted client could use them to drive
unbounded CPU, GPU or memory use. Server-level --mm-processor-kwargs and
--media-io-kwargs are unaffected.

This changes default behavior: a client that sends either field gets a 400
until the server opts in.

Carried: every vllm/ hunk, unchanged. They apply to v0.30.0 with line offsets
only. The gate sits in OnlineRenderer.preprocess_chat and preprocess_cmpl
(chat, completion, Responses, tokenize, render and batch requests) and in
PoolingBaseServing._init_ctx (pooling and scoring requests), the same entry
points as upstream.

Not carried: docs/usage/security.md, the upstream tests, and
rust/src/cmd/src/cli/unsupported.rs (this package does not build the Rust
frontend).

Drop at the first packaged vLLM release that contains 31f2e70c.

---
